    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5a196a7e-002d-566c-b45e-934ff02b2d7b",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)<7$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 7$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=7 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe given full column space implies that $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=7$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $A\\text{ is invertible}$. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false: $\\text{rank}(A)<7$. $\\text{rank}(A)=7$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\n- Statement III is true: $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 7$. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and III only.",
